### VS Code REST Client Tests
### Install "REST Client" extension by Huachao Mao
### Then click "Send Request" above each request

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@apiKey = your-api-key-here
@userId = test-user

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### 2. Create API Key
POST {{baseUrl}}/apikey
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "provider": "openrouter",
  "api_key": "sk-or-v1-your-openrouter-key"
}

### 3. List Available Skills (should show 1,080+ skills)
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### 4. List Available Tools (should show 50+ tools)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tools
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### 5. Simple Chat Request (Enhanced API)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Debug my Python API performance issues",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "workspace",
  "context_key": "test-project"
}

### 6. Chat with Specific Skill
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Analyze this React component for performance",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "skill_name": "frontend_debug",
  "memory_scope": "workspace",
  "context_key": "my-react-app"
}

### 7. Research with Web Search
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "What are the latest React 19 features?",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "user"
}

### 8. Code Analysis
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Review this Python code for security issues: def login(username, password): return db.execute(f'SELECT * FROM users WHERE username={username}')",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "workspace",
  "context_key": "security-review"
}

### 9. Store Memory
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/memory
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "text": "User prefers concise JSON responses",
  "kind": "preference",
  "memory_scope": "user",
  "metadata": {
    "source": "manual"
  }
}

### 10. Retrieve Memory Context
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/memory/context?user_id={{userId}}&memory_scope=user&query=preferences
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### 11. Run Specific Tool
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tools/web_search
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "Python async best practices 2024"
}

### 12. Streaming Request (copy URL to browser or use EventSource)
# Open in browser: http://localhost:8000/stream/chat
# Or use the frontend for visual streaming

### 13. Compare: Normal OpenRouter vs Enhanced
# First, run normal OpenRouter (replace with your key):
POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer sk-or-v1-your-key
Content-Type: application/json
HTTP-Referer: http://localhost
X-Title: API Test

{
  "model": "openrouter/free",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Debug my Python API performance issues"
    }
  ]
}

### Then run Enhanced API (same prompt):
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Debug my Python API performance issues",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "workspace",
  "context_key": "test-project"
}

### 14. Test Cross-API-Key Memory
# Create second API key
POST {{baseUrl}}/apikey
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "provider": "openrouter",
  "api_key": "sk-or-v1-second-key"
}

# Use first API key to store preference
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Remember: I prefer JSON responses",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "user"
}

# Use second API key - should remember preference
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer sk-or-v1-second-key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Show me user statistics",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "user"
}

### 15. Test Skill Routing Accuracy
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Write a SQL query to find top 10 customers by revenue",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}"
}
# Should route to: database_* or sql_* skill

### 16. Test Tool Execution
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Search for the latest TypeScript 5.3 features and summarize",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}"
}
# Should execute: web_search tool

### 17. Test Complex Task with Multiple Tools
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Research GraphQL vs REST performance, analyze the trade-offs, and recommend which to use for a high-traffic API",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "workspace",
  "context_key": "architecture-decisions"
}
# Should execute: web_search, deep_search
# Should route to: backend_architect or research skill

### 18. Test Memory Persistence
# First request
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "I'm working on an e-commerce platform using Next.js and PostgreSQL",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "workspace",
  "context_key": "my-ecommerce-project"
}

# Second request (should remember context)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "How should I optimize the database queries?",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "memory_scope": "workspace",
  "context_key": "my-ecommerce-project"
}
# Should remember: Next.js + PostgreSQL context

### 19. Test Cost Tracking
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/run
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "input": "Explain how async/await works in JavaScript",
  "user_id": "{{userId}}"
}
# Check response.usage for cost tracking

### 20. Batch Test - Run Multiple Requests
# You can select multiple requests and click "Send Request" for each
